data.falsifiable_test:
Run on full val (n=750) with the same starts as P-001 and P-013, and compute paired bootstrap 95% CIs on per-sample squared-error differences. The hypothesis is falsified if any of the following holds:
(a) val rel_l2 >= 0.022;
(b) the CI of [rel_l2(P-001) - rel_l2(P-009)] lies entirely below 0, meaning more draws hurt;
(c) the CI of [rel_l2(P-013) - rel_l2(P-009)] lies entirely at or below 0, meaning the mode is at least as good as a low-MC-noise mean;
(d) in the stratum with k1 or k4 within 10% of a bound, the mode-minus-mean gain is not larger than in the complementary stratum.
Also report the per-sample ESS distribution and the IS MC standard error.

